  "authority_invariants": [
    "Jarvis Core remains authoritative for durable memory, tools, permissions, tasks, runtime state, private/current application data, and backend routing",
    "Realtime Mini is a replaceable conversational frontend; it may answer ordinary conversation directly but does not become durable Jarvis authority",
    "delegate_to_jarvis_core expresses a goal/reason for delegation and never selects the concrete backend model/provider",
    "Core may later route delegated work to Luna, Sol, local/future providers, tools, memory, current-data services, or task workers without changing the conversational frontend",
    "WebRTC is the preferred user-device media transport; browser is only the 0.0.9 lab harness and may be embedded in Electron/React later",
    "GPT-Live, full Realtime 2.1, raw WebSocket/server transport, and the local Whisper/Qwen pipeline remain retained alternatives/fallbacks",
    "newer delegated corrections suppress stale backend results while Core retains cooperative cancellation authority"
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
